{"items":[{"title":"German Electoral Studies (Wahlstudien)","url_or_doi":"https://doi.org/10.48488/68778","justification":"The Wahlstudien series includes data from the 1970s covering political attitudes, voting behavior, and party preferences in Germany. While not solely focused on governmental organizations, it provides crucial context on the political landscape influencing them."},
{"title":"Political Attitudes and Behavior in West Germany 1972-1980","url_or_doi":"https://doi.org/10.48488/14347","justification":"This dataset directly addresses political attitudes and behavior during much of the 1970s in West Germany, informing understanding of the environment in which the government and political systems operated."},
{"title":"Infratest public opinion polls","url_or_doi":"https://doi.org/10.48488/22896","justification":"GESIS hosts a collection of Infratest polls, some of which cover the 1970s and provide insights into public opinion on political issues, government performance, and key political actors."},
{"title":"Data on Political Participation in Germany","url_or_doi":"https://doi.org/10.48488/12068","justification":"This dataset, while spanning a wider timeframe, includes variables relevant to the 1970s and measures various forms of political participation, offering clues about civic engagement with the government and political systems."},
{"title":"Social Report Germany (Sozialbericht Deutschland)","url_or_doi":"https://doi.org/10.48488/71064","justification":"While broad in scope, the Sozialbericht contains information related to social and political developments in Germany, and historical editions from the 1970s would offer data on the context of governmental actions and societal changes."},
{"title":"Membership Surveys of Interest Groups (Mitgliederbefragungen von Interessenverbänden)","url_or_doi":"https://doi.org/10.48488/61324","justification":"These surveys, when available for the 1970s, provide data about the interests represented to the government and the opinions of specific organized groups, shedding light on the interplay between organizations and the political system."},
{"title":"European Social Survey (ESS) - Cross-national time series data.","url_or_doi":"https://doi.org/10.48488/19185","justification":"Though the ESS began later, earlier rounds include retrospective questions or data series extending back into the 1970s. Contains variables related to political trust, political interest and engagement which are useful when studying political systems and organizations."}
]}
